' A real, self-contained x86-64 instruction ENCODER, ported (as a real
' ArcoBASIC implementation, per this project's own "First-party Fission
' implementation should be ArcoBASIC wherever technically possible" rule)
' from the byte-level encoding techniques legacy ArcoFission itself
' already proved out (systems::x86_64::Assembler, arcology-os/include/
' arco/x86_64_encoder.hpp -- REX-prefix/ModRM/SIB bit patterns verified
' there against `nasm -f bin` output). This exists specifically because
' Arcology is meant to be a self-contained ecosystem: this substrate's
' native x86-64 backend previously rendered GAS assembly TEXT and shelled
' out to the system `as`/`ld` toolchain to reach a final ELF64 -- a real
' external-tool dependency for something as central as "compile ArcoBASIC
' to a native executable," called out directly by the project owner
' ("we're passing stuff to GAS... port the machine code gen from legacy
' fission").
'
' A genuinely useful finding while scoping this: legacy ArcoFission's OWN
' Linux native backend also ends up shelling out to `as`/`ld` for the final
' ELF64 (`render_x86_64_linux_asm`, src/compiler/fission.cpp) -- its own
' byte-level encoder only ever reaches an in-memory instruction stream
' (used directly by its JIT), then gets rendered BACK to GAS text and
' handed to `as`/`ld` for two things it explicitly declined to reimplement:
' resolving calls into an external runtime shim, and general ELF section
' layout/alignment.
'
' Scope: exactly the ~40 instruction mnemonics/operand shapes
' fission/amir/lower_x86_64.abas's own codegen actually emits (confirmed
' directly against every real fission/tests/native_programs/*.abas
' fixture's own rendered assembly text, not assumed) -- this is
' deliberately NOT a general x86-64 assembler. Every memory operand is
' encoded using the WIDEST safe form (disp32, never disp8; rel32 jumps/
' calls, never the short rel8 form) rather than a real assembler's own
' size-minimizing relaxation -- code density is not a goal anywhere in this
' project, and a single fixed-width encoding per instruction shape means
' every instruction's own byte length is known immediately during a single
' encoding pass, with no iterative relaxation needed at all.
'
' This file's own job ends at producing a real, independent FRAGMENT (see
' fission/amir/x86_64_fragment.abas) -- text/rodata bytes, a symbol table,
' and a relocation list -- not a final ELF64 executable. That used to be
' one combined pass (encode text, then immediately resolve every label's
' own final virtual address and write the ELF64 header), but the encoder
' and the linker are genuinely separate concerns: encoding an instruction
' needs no idea what the FINAL address of anything will be, and linking
' needs no idea how any individual instruction got encoded. Splitting them
' -- requested directly by the project owner -- means a real, independent
' object-file format (fragments) and a real, separately-named linker
' (fission/amir/fusion_linker.abas, "The Arcology Fusion Linker") now
' exist, setting up for genuine per-file incremental native compilation
' later (each ArcoBASIC file compiles to its own cached fragment once,
' only the final link step re-runs when something changes -- the same
' "why rebuild" causality Rivet already proved for C++). This file itself
' needed NO changes to its own instruction-encoding logic at all for this
' split -- only its own driver function (Fission_X86_64AssembleFragment,
' at the bottom of this file) changed, from "resolve+write the final
' ELF64" to "package up what was encoded into a fragment and hand it to
' whoever asked for it."
'
' fission/amir/lower_x86_64.abas's OWN codegen logic (which A-MIR
' instruction becomes which x86 operation) is completely unchanged by any
' of this -- it still renders the exact same text lines as always; this
' file just parses that text (a small, fully self-defined dialect, not
' general GAS syntax) into real machine code bytes.

#IMPORT "fission/core/diagnostics.abas"
#IMPORT "fission/amir/x86_64_fragment.abas"

FUNCTION Fission_X86_64AsmRegisterIndex(name)
    table = {rax: 0, rcx: 1, rdx: 2, rbx: 3, rsp: 4, rbp: 5, rsi: 6, rdi: 7,
             r8: 8, r9: 9, r10: 10, r11: 11, r12: 12, r13: 13, r14: 14, r15: 15}
    RETURN Object.Get(table, name, -1)
END FUNCTION

' Byte-sized register names this backend's own codegen actually emits:
' the four legacy byte registers (al/cl/dl -- never bl, never the
' high-byte ah/ch/dh/bh forms, and never spl/bpl/sil/dil, none of which
' this backend's own codegen ever needs) plus the numbered r8b..r15b
' forms (always available with no legacy ambiguity, unlike al/cl/dl).
' Returns {Index, IsByteReg} or NULL if `name` isn't a recognized register
' token at all.
FUNCTION Fission_X86_64AsmParseRegisterToken(token)
    name = token
    IF String.StartsWith(name, "%") THEN name = String.Slice(name, 1, String.Length(name) - 1)
    byteTable = {al: 0, cl: 1, dl: 2, bl: 3}
    byteIndex = Object.Get(byteTable, name, -1)
    IF byteIndex >= 0 THEN RETURN {Index: byteIndex, IsByteReg: TRUE}
    IF String.EndsWith(name, "b") ANDALSO String.StartsWith(name, "r") THEN
        wideName = String.Slice(name, 0, String.Length(name) - 1)
        wideIndex = Fission_X86_64AsmRegisterIndex(wideName)
        IF wideIndex >= 8 THEN RETURN {Index: wideIndex, IsByteReg: TRUE}
    END IF
    plainIndex = Fission_X86_64AsmRegisterIndex(name)
    IF plainIndex >= 0 THEN RETURN {Index: plainIndex, IsByteReg: FALSE}
    RETURN NULL
END FUNCTION

' FissionX86_64Buffer itself now lives in fission/amir/x86_64_fragment.abas
' (imported above) -- a real, growing byte buffer plus little-endian
' Emit*/PatchU32 helpers, unchanged in every particular from before this
' file was split, just relocated to the lowest-level file in this
' backend's own dependency graph so fission/amir/fusion_linker.abas can
' use it too without depending on this encoder at all.

FUNCTION Fission_X86_64AsmFitsSigned32(value)
    RETURN value >= -2147483648 ANDALSO value <= 2147483647
END FUNCTION

' REX prefix -- 0100WRXB. Omitted entirely (real assemblers do this too)
' when none of W/R/X/B are needed, exactly matching legacy's own byte
' output for e.g. a bare `movb (%rdi), %al` (no REX at all).
FUNCTION Fission_X86_64AsmRex(w, regIndex, indexRegIndex, rmIndex)
    r = 0
    IF regIndex >= 8 THEN r = 1
    x = 0
    IF indexRegIndex >= 8 THEN x = 1
    b = 0
    IF rmIndex >= 8 THEN b = 1
    IF w == 0 ANDALSO r == 0 ANDALSO x == 0 ANDALSO b == 0 THEN RETURN -1
    RETURN 64 BITOR (w SHL 3) BITOR (r SHL 2) BITOR (x SHL 1) BITOR b
END FUNCTION

FUNCTION Fission_X86_64AsmEmitRex(buffer, w, regIndex, indexRegIndex, rmIndex)
    rex = Fission_X86_64AsmRex(w, regIndex, indexRegIndex, rmIndex)
    IF rex >= 0 THEN ignored = buffer.EmitByte(rex)
END FUNCTION

' A parsed operand -- exactly one of:
'   {Kind: "reg", Index, IsByteReg}
'   {Kind: "imm", Value}
'   {Kind: "mem", Base, HasIndex, Index, Scale, Disp}   -- Base/Index are
'       register indices; HasIndex FALSE means a plain [Base+Disp] operand
'   {Kind: "riprel", Label}                              -- LABEL(%rip)
'   {Kind: "label", Name}                                -- a bare jmp/call
'       target with no `%`/`$`/`(` at all
FUNCTION Fission_X86_64AsmParseOperand(token)
    trimmed = String.Trim(token)
    IF String.StartsWith(trimmed, "$") THEN
        RETURN {Kind: "imm", Value: NUMBER(String.Slice(trimmed, 1, String.Length(trimmed) - 1))}
    END IF
    IF String.EndsWith(trimmed, "(%rip)") THEN
        label = String.Slice(trimmed, 0, String.Length(trimmed) - 6)
        RETURN {Kind: "riprel", Label: label}
    END IF
    IF String.Contains(trimmed, "(") THEN
        parenIndex = String.IndexOf(trimmed, "(")
        dispText = String.Trim(String.Slice(trimmed, 0, parenIndex))
        disp = 0
        IF dispText != "" THEN disp = NUMBER(dispText)
        inner = String.Slice(trimmed, parenIndex + 1, String.Length(trimmed) - parenIndex - 2)
        parts = Fission_X86_64AsmSplitTopLevel(inner, ",")
        baseReg = Fission_X86_64AsmParseRegisterToken(String.Trim(parts[0]))
        IF LEN(parts) == 1 THEN
            RETURN {Kind: "mem", Base: baseReg.Index, HasIndex: FALSE, Index: -1, Scale: 1, Disp: disp}
        END IF
        indexReg = Fission_X86_64AsmParseRegisterToken(String.Trim(parts[1]))
        scale = NUMBER(String.Trim(parts[2]))
        RETURN {Kind: "mem", Base: baseReg.Index, HasIndex: TRUE, Index: indexReg.Index, Scale: scale, Disp: disp}
    END IF
    IF String.StartsWith(trimmed, "%") THEN
        reg = Fission_X86_64AsmParseRegisterToken(trimmed)
        RETURN {Kind: "reg", Index: reg.Index, IsByteReg: reg.IsByteReg}
    END IF
    RETURN {Kind: "label", Name: trimmed}
END FUNCTION

' Splits `text` on `sep` at PAREN-DEPTH ZERO ONLY -- needed because a SIB
' memory operand's own inner "base,index,scale" list (e.g.
' "8(%rax,%rcx,8)") contains commas that must NOT be treated as operand
' separators when splitting a whole instruction's operand list, and this
' same splitter is reused (with `,` as `sep`) for that inner list too, once
' the outer parens have already been stripped down to just "rax,rcx,8".
FUNCTION Fission_X86_64AsmSplitTopLevel(text, sep)
    parts = []
    current = ""
    depth = 0
    chars = String.ToChars(text)
    sepLen = String.Length(sep)
    index = 0
    WHILE index < LEN(chars)
        ch = chars[index]
        IF ch == "(" THEN depth = depth + 1
        IF ch == ")" THEN depth = depth - 1
        matchesSep = FALSE
        IF depth == 0 ANDALSO index + sepLen <= LEN(chars) THEN
            candidate = String.Slice(text, index, sepLen)
            IF candidate == sep THEN matchesSep = TRUE
        END IF
        IF matchesSep THEN
            ignored = Array.Push(parts, current)
            current = ""
            index = index + sepLen
            CONTINUE WHILE
        END IF
        current = current + ch
        index = index + 1
    WEND
    ignored = Array.Push(parts, current)
    RETURN parts
END FUNCTION

' A memory (or register-direct) operand's ModRM[+SIB][+disp32] bytes,
' given the OTHER operand's register index for the ModRM.reg field (per
' the real x86-64 "/r" convention every instruction below uses). Always
' the widest safe form: mod=11 for a bare register, otherwise ALWAYS
' mod=10 (disp32), even for a zero or small displacement, and a SIB byte
' whenever the base register is RSP/R12 (whose low 3 bits collide with
' "SIB follows") or an explicit index register is present -- one uniform
' code path with no smaller-encoding special cases to get wrong.
FUNCTION Fission_X86_64AsmEmitModRM(buffer, regField, rm)
    IF rm.Kind == "reg" THEN
        modrm = 192 BITOR ((regField BITAND 7) SHL 3) BITOR (rm.Index BITAND 7)
        ignored = buffer.EmitByte(modrm)
        RETURN
    END IF
    IF rm.Kind == "riprel" THEN
        modrm = ((regField BITAND 7) SHL 3) BITOR 5
        ignored = buffer.EmitByte(modrm)
        ignored = buffer.EmitU32(0)
        RETURN
    END IF
    ' rm.Kind == "mem"
    baseLow3 = rm.Base BITAND 7
    needsSib = rm.HasIndex ORELSE baseLow3 == 4
    rmField = 4
    IF needsSib == FALSE THEN rmField = baseLow3
    modrm = 128 BITOR ((regField BITAND 7) SHL 3) BITOR rmField
    ignored = buffer.EmitByte(modrm)
    IF needsSib THEN
        indexLow3 = 4
        IF rm.HasIndex THEN indexLow3 = rm.Index BITAND 7
        scaleBits = 0
        IF rm.HasIndex THEN
            IF rm.Scale == 2 THEN scaleBits = 1
            IF rm.Scale == 4 THEN scaleBits = 2
            IF rm.Scale == 8 THEN scaleBits = 3
        END IF
        sib = (scaleBits SHL 6) BITOR (indexLow3 SHL 3) BITOR baseLow3
        ignored = buffer.EmitByte(sib)
    END IF
    ignored = buffer.EmitU32(rm.Disp)
END FUNCTION

' The register-extension bits an `rm` operand contributes to REX.X/REX.B --
' 0 for anything that isn't a "mem" operand with an extended base/index
' register (a bare "reg" operand's own extension is handled by the caller
' via its own regIndex, and "riprel"/"label" operands never need REX.X/B
' at all since RIP-relative addressing has no base/index register).
FUNCTION Fission_X86_64AsmRmIndexBits(rm)
    IF rm.Kind == "mem" THEN
        indexBit = -1
        IF rm.HasIndex THEN indexBit = rm.Index
        RETURN {Base: rm.Base, Index: indexBit}
    END IF
    IF rm.Kind == "reg" THEN RETURN {Base: rm.Index, Index: -1}
    RETURN {Base: -1, Index: -1}
END FUNCTION

' Encodes a standard 2-operand "opcode /r" instruction where `regOperand`
' (a bare register) fills ModRM.reg and `rmOperand` (register or memory)
' fills ModRM.rm/SIB/disp32 -- the shape shared by mov/add/sub/and/or/xor/
' cmp/test/movzx and friends below. `w` selects REX.W (64-bit operand
' size); byte-sized forms (movb/cmpb/testb and any instruction using an
' 8-bit register) pass w=0.
FUNCTION Fission_X86_64AsmEmitRegRm(buffer, w, opcodeBytes, regIndex, rm)
    rmBits = Fission_X86_64AsmRmIndexBits(rm)
    ignored = Fission_X86_64AsmEmitRex(buffer, w, regIndex, rmBits.Index, rmBits.Base)
    FOR b IN opcodeBytes
        ignored = buffer.EmitByte(b)
    NEXT
    ignored = Fission_X86_64AsmEmitModRM(buffer, regIndex, rm)
END FUNCTION

' A relative-displacement fixup: patched once every label's own final
' address is known. `FieldOffset` is the byte offset (in the FINAL,
' combined text+rodata buffer -- see Fission_X86_64Assemble) of the first
' byte of the 4-byte field to patch; the real x86-64 rule for BOTH a near
' JMP/Jcc/CALL's rel32 and a RIP-relative LEA's own disp32 is identical:
' `target_address - (address_of_the_byte_immediately_after_this_field)`,
' so one fixup shape covers both cases.
FUNCTION FissionX86_64Fixup(fieldOffset, targetLabel)
    RETURN {FieldOffset: fieldOffset, Target: targetLabel}
END FUNCTION

' The whole per-instruction dispatcher: given a mnemonic and its already-
' top-level-split operand tokens, appends real bytes to `buffer` and
' records any fixup needed (a jmp/call/lea whose target is a label defined
' elsewhere in this same program) into `fixups`. `currentOffset()` is a
' function the caller supplies to read the buffer's own length at the
' moment a fixup is recorded, since PushLoop-style closures aren't needed
' here -- `buffer.Length()` is passed directly instead.
FUNCTION Fission_X86_64AsmEncodeInstruction(buffer, fixups, diagnostics, mnemonic, operandTokens)
    operands = []
    FOR token IN operandTokens
        ignored = Array.Push(operands, Fission_X86_64AsmParseOperand(token))
    NEXT

    ' "op $N, dst" -- an immediate first operand (`sub $16, %rsp`,
    ' `add $8, %rsp`, `xor $1, %rax`), a genuinely different encoding
    ' family (81 /ext id) from the register/memory "op src, dst" form
    ' below, checked first since add/sub/and/or/xor/cmp all share the same
    ' mnemonic between both forms and only the FIRST operand's own kind
    ' tells them apart.
    immExtOpcodes = {"add": 0, "or": 1, "and": 4, "sub": 5, "xor": 6, "cmp": 7}
    IF Object.Has(immExtOpcodes, mnemonic) ANDALSO LEN(operands) == 2 ANDALSO operands[0].Kind == "imm" THEN
        ext = Object.Get(immExtOpcodes, mnemonic, 0)
        dst = operands[1]
        rmBits = Fission_X86_64AsmRmIndexBits(dst)
        ignored = Fission_X86_64AsmEmitRex(buffer, 1, 0, -1, rmBits.Base)
        ignored = buffer.EmitByte(129)
        ignored = Fission_X86_64AsmEmitModRM(buffer, ext, dst)
        ignored = buffer.EmitU32(operands[0].Value)
        RETURN
    END IF

    ' Plain register-register / register-memory "op src, dst" family --
    ' AT&T order: ModRM.reg = SRC (1st operand), ModRM.rm = DST (2nd).
    ' Two opcode tables since a byte-register pair (only ever `cmp %al,
    ' %cl`-shaped in this backend's own real codegen, but handled
    ' generally rather than special-cased to just that one mnemonic) needs
    ' the byte-sized opcode family and REX.W=0, not the 64-bit family.
    binaryOpcodes = {"add": [1], "sub": [41], "and": [33], "or": [9], "xor": [49], "cmp": [57], "test": [133]}
    binaryOpcodesByte = {"add": [0], "sub": [40], "and": [32], "or": [8], "xor": [48], "cmp": [56], "test": [132]}
    IF Object.Has(binaryOpcodes, mnemonic) THEN
        src = operands[0]
        dst = operands[1]
        isByte = (src.Kind == "reg" ANDALSO src.IsByteReg) ORELSE (dst.Kind == "reg" ANDALSO dst.IsByteReg)
        opcode = Object.Get(binaryOpcodes, mnemonic, [])
        w = 1
        IF isByte THEN
            opcode = Object.Get(binaryOpcodesByte, mnemonic, [])
            w = 0
        END IF
        regIndex = src.Index
        IF dst.Kind == "reg" ANDALSO src.Kind == "mem" THEN
            ' A memory source with a register dest still needs the "load"
            ' direction bit for cmp/test to read correctly -- but every
            ' real use in this backend's own codegen keeps the register
            ' operand as ModRM.reg regardless of which side loads, since
            ' the encoded FLAGS/result is symmetric for cmp/test and the
            ' other binaryOpcodes members never see a bare memory operand
            ' at all in this backend's own generated text.
            regIndex = dst.Index
        END IF
        ignored = Fission_X86_64AsmEmitRegRm(buffer, w, opcode, regIndex, dst)
        RETURN
    END IF

    ' `movq $N, disp(%rbp)`-shaped: an immediate stored directly to a
    ' memory operand, with an explicit `q` (quadword) size suffix since
    ' unlike every other `mov` this backend emits, there is no register
    ' operand at all to make the 64-bit operand size unambiguous. Byte-
    ' identical encoding to the "mov" immediate-to-memory case below (C7
    ' /0 id), just reached under a different mnemonic spelling.
    IF mnemonic == "mov" ORELSE mnemonic == "movq" THEN
        src = operands[0]
        dst = operands[1]
        IF src.Kind == "imm" THEN
            IF Fission_X86_64AsmFitsSigned32(src.Value) THEN
                ' C7 /0 id -- MOV r/m64, imm32 (sign-extended). Works
                ' identically whether dst is a register (mod=11) or a
                ' memory operand (mod=10 disp32 then the imm32 value)
                ' since Fission_X86_64AsmEmitModRM already handles both
                ' uniformly.
                rmBits = Fission_X86_64AsmRmIndexBits(dst)
                ignored = Fission_X86_64AsmEmitRex(buffer, 1, 0, -1, rmBits.Base)
                ignored = buffer.EmitByte(199)
                ignored = Fission_X86_64AsmEmitModRM(buffer, 0, dst)
                ignored = buffer.EmitU32(src.Value)
                RETURN
            END IF
            ' A real, PREVIOUSLY genuinely-crashing bug: an immediate
            ' outside the signed 32-bit range (e.g. `mov $4294967295,
            ' %rax`) has no correct encoding via C7 /0 id at all -- that
            ' opcode's own imm32 operand is ALWAYS sign-extended into the
            ' 64-bit destination, a real x86-64 ISA constraint, not a
            ' choice this backend made (confirmed directly: this exact
            ' bug made `PRINT 4294967295` silently print `-1`, and made
            ' `Random.Integer(0, 4294967295, h)` crash with SIGFPE
            ' downstream). A register destination has a real, correct
            ' full-width encoding instead: REX.W + B8+rd io (`MOV r64,
            ' imm64`, 10 bytes, no sign-extension at all) --
            ' Fission_X86_64AsmFitsSigned32/FissionX86_64Buffer's own
            ' EmitU64Full already existed for exactly this, just never
            ' wired into this dispatch until now.
            IF dst.Kind == "reg" THEN
                ignored = Fission_X86_64AsmEmitRex(buffer, 1, 0, -1, dst.Index)
                ignored = buffer.EmitByte(184 + (dst.Index BITAND 7))
                ignored = buffer.EmitU64Full(src.Value)
                RETURN
            END IF
            ' A memory destination has NO real 64-bit-immediate MOV
            ' encoding on x86-64 at all (there is no `MOV r/m64, imm64`);
            ' the correct real fix there is loading into a scratch
            ' register first and storing that, but this codegen never
            ' actually needs that shape (every literal this backend emits
            ' reaches memory only via a register first -- see
            ' Fission_X86_64OperandLoadLine/Fission_X86_64StoreRaxLine) --
            ' a real, reported diagnostic here instead of silently
            ' truncating, matching this whole file's own "diagnose an
            ' unsupported shape rather than mis-encode it" discipline
            ' (the RIP-relative-source case right below already does the
            ' same).
            ignored = diagnostics.ReportError("FISSION_X86_64_ASM_UNSUPPORTED", "mov with a 64-bit immediate directly to memory is not supported")
            RETURN
        END IF
        IF src.Kind == "riprel" THEN
            ' Never actually emitted (`lea`, not `mov`, is always used for
            ' a label reference in this backend's own codegen) but handled
            ' for completeness/robustness rather than silently mis-encoding
            ' it if that ever changes.
            ignored = diagnostics.ReportError("FISSION_X86_64_ASM_UNSUPPORTED", "mov with a RIP-relative source is not supported")
            RETURN
        END IF
        IF src.Kind == "reg" ANDALSO dst.Kind == "reg" THEN
            IF src.IsByteReg THEN
                ignored = Fission_X86_64AsmEmitRegRm(buffer, 0, [136], src.Index, dst)
            ELSE
                ignored = Fission_X86_64AsmEmitRegRm(buffer, 1, [137], src.Index, dst)
            END IF
            RETURN
        END IF
        IF src.Kind == "reg" ANDALSO dst.Kind == "mem" THEN
            ' Store: reg -> memory.
            IF src.IsByteReg THEN
                ignored = Fission_X86_64AsmEmitRegRm(buffer, 0, [136], src.Index, dst)
            ELSE
                ignored = Fission_X86_64AsmEmitRegRm(buffer, 1, [137], src.Index, dst)
            END IF
            RETURN
        END IF
        IF src.Kind == "mem" ANDALSO dst.Kind == "reg" THEN
            ' Load: memory -> reg.
            IF dst.IsByteReg THEN
                ignored = Fission_X86_64AsmEmitRegRm(buffer, 0, [138], dst.Index, src)
            ELSE
                ignored = Fission_X86_64AsmEmitRegRm(buffer, 1, [139], dst.Index, src)
            END IF
            RETURN
        END IF
        ignored = diagnostics.ReportError("FISSION_X86_64_ASM_UNSUPPORTED", "Unsupported mov operand combination")
        RETURN
    END IF

    IF mnemonic == "movb" THEN
        src = operands[0]
        dst = operands[1]
        IF src.Kind == "imm" THEN
            ' C6 /0 ib -- MOV r/m8, imm8.
            rmBits = Fission_X86_64AsmRmIndexBits(dst)
            ignored = Fission_X86_64AsmEmitRex(buffer, 0, 0, -1, rmBits.Base)
            ignored = buffer.EmitByte(198)
            ignored = Fission_X86_64AsmEmitModRM(buffer, 0, dst)
            ignored = buffer.EmitByte(src.Value)
            RETURN
        END IF
        IF dst.Kind == "reg" THEN
            ignored = Fission_X86_64AsmEmitRegRm(buffer, 0, [138], dst.Index, src)
        ELSE
            ignored = Fission_X86_64AsmEmitRegRm(buffer, 0, [136], src.Index, dst)
        END IF
        RETURN
    END IF

    IF mnemonic == "movzbq" THEN
        src = operands[0]
        dst = operands[1]
        ignored = Fission_X86_64AsmEmitRegRm(buffer, 1, [15, 182], dst.Index, src)
        RETURN
    END IF

    IF mnemonic == "cmpb" THEN
        left = operands[0]
        right = operands[1]
        IF left.Kind == "imm" THEN
            ' 80 /7 ib -- CMP r/m8, imm8 (right is the memory operand).
            rmBits = Fission_X86_64AsmRmIndexBits(right)
            ignored = Fission_X86_64AsmEmitRex(buffer, 0, 0, -1, rmBits.Base)
            ignored = buffer.EmitByte(128)
            ignored = Fission_X86_64AsmEmitModRM(buffer, 7, right)
            ignored = buffer.EmitByte(left.Value)
            RETURN
        END IF
        ignored = diagnostics.ReportError("FISSION_X86_64_ASM_UNSUPPORTED", "Unsupported cmpb operand combination")
        RETURN
    END IF

    IF mnemonic == "testb" THEN
        left = operands[0]
        right = operands[1]
        ignored = Fission_X86_64AsmEmitRegRm(buffer, 0, [132], left.Index, right)
        RETURN
    END IF

    IF mnemonic == "imul" THEN
        src = operands[0]
        dst = operands[1]
        ignored = Fission_X86_64AsmEmitRegRm(buffer, 1, [15, 175], dst.Index, src)
        RETURN
    END IF

    IF mnemonic == "cqto" THEN
        ignored = buffer.EmitByte(72)
        ignored = buffer.EmitByte(153)
        RETURN
    END IF

    ' Group 3 (opcode F7 /ext) -- idiv/div/neg/not. A real, caught-by-
    ' running-the-code bug found here: inc/dec were originally grouped into
    ' this SAME F7 opcode table, but INC/DEC r/m64 is a genuinely different
    ' opcode (Group 5, FF /0 and /1 respectively) -- F7 /0 is actually
    ' TEST r/m,imm32, so `inc %rax` was being mis-encoded as a 7-byte TEST
    ' instruction with garbage trailing bytes, corrupting everything after
    ' it (confirmed via objdump on the real emitted bytes: a `test
    ' rax,0xffffffffffffebe9` where a plain 3-byte `inc rax` belonged,
    ' followed by a SIGILL when the corrupted instruction stream was
    ' actually executed). Split into its own Group 5 table below instead
    ' of trusting the two families share an opcode just because both are
    ' "unary register operand" shaped.
    group3Opcodes = {"idiv": 7, "div": 6, "neg": 3, "not": 2}
    IF Object.Has(group3Opcodes, mnemonic) THEN
        ext = Object.Get(group3Opcodes, mnemonic, 0)
        rm = operands[0]
        rmBits = Fission_X86_64AsmRmIndexBits(rm)
        ignored = Fission_X86_64AsmEmitRex(buffer, 1, 0, -1, rmBits.Base)
        ignored = buffer.EmitByte(247)
        ignored = Fission_X86_64AsmEmitModRM(buffer, ext, rm)
        RETURN
    END IF
    group5Opcodes = {"inc": 0, "dec": 1}
    IF Object.Has(group5Opcodes, mnemonic) THEN
        ext = Object.Get(group5Opcodes, mnemonic, 0)
        rm = operands[0]
        rmBits = Fission_X86_64AsmRmIndexBits(rm)
        ignored = Fission_X86_64AsmEmitRex(buffer, 1, 0, -1, rmBits.Base)
        ignored = buffer.EmitByte(255)
        ignored = Fission_X86_64AsmEmitModRM(buffer, ext, rm)
        RETURN
    END IF

    IF mnemonic == "push" THEN
        operand = operands[0]
        IF operand.Kind == "reg" THEN
            IF operand.Index >= 8 THEN ignored = buffer.EmitByte(65)
            ignored = buffer.EmitByte(80 + (operand.Index BITAND 7))
            RETURN
        END IF
        ' push m64 -- FF /6.
        rmBits = Fission_X86_64AsmRmIndexBits(operand)
        ignored = Fission_X86_64AsmEmitRex(buffer, 0, 0, -1, rmBits.Base)
        ignored = buffer.EmitByte(255)
        ignored = Fission_X86_64AsmEmitModRM(buffer, 6, operand)
        RETURN
    END IF
    IF mnemonic == "pop" THEN
        operand = operands[0]
        IF operand.Index >= 8 THEN ignored = buffer.EmitByte(65)
        ignored = buffer.EmitByte(88 + (operand.Index BITAND 7))
        RETURN
    END IF

    IF mnemonic == "lea" THEN
        src = operands[0]
        dst = operands[1]
        IF src.Kind == "riprel" THEN
            rmBits = Fission_X86_64AsmRmIndexBits(src)
            ignored = Fission_X86_64AsmEmitRex(buffer, 1, dst.Index, rmBits.Index, rmBits.Base)
            ignored = buffer.EmitByte(141)
            fieldOffset = buffer.Length() + 1
            ignored = Fission_X86_64AsmEmitModRM(buffer, dst.Index, src)
            ignored = Array.Push(fixups, FissionX86_64Fixup(fieldOffset, src.Label))
            RETURN
        END IF
        ignored = Fission_X86_64AsmEmitRegRm(buffer, 1, [141], dst.Index, src)
        RETURN
    END IF

    setccOpcodes = {"sete": 148, "setne": 149, "setl": 156, "setle": 158, "setg": 159, "setge": 157}
    IF Object.Has(setccOpcodes, mnemonic) THEN
        opcode = Object.Get(setccOpcodes, mnemonic, 148)
        operand = operands[0]
        IF operand.Index >= 8 THEN ignored = buffer.EmitByte(65)
        ignored = buffer.EmitByte(15)
        ignored = buffer.EmitByte(opcode)
        ignored = buffer.EmitByte(192 BITOR (operand.Index BITAND 7))
        RETURN
    END IF

    shiftImmOpcodes = {"shl": 4, "sar": 7, "shr": 5}
    IF Object.Has(shiftImmOpcodes, mnemonic) THEN
        ext = Object.Get(shiftImmOpcodes, mnemonic, 4)
        left = operands[0]
        right = operands[1]
        IF left.Kind == "imm" THEN
            rmBits = Fission_X86_64AsmRmIndexBits(right)
            ignored = Fission_X86_64AsmEmitRex(buffer, 1, 0, -1, rmBits.Base)
            ignored = buffer.EmitByte(193)
            ignored = Fission_X86_64AsmEmitModRM(buffer, ext, right)
            ignored = buffer.EmitByte(left.Value)
            RETURN
        END IF
        ' %cl, reg -- D3 /ext, the CPU implicitly uses CL, not encoded in
        ' the ModRM at all.
        rmBits = Fission_X86_64AsmRmIndexBits(right)
        ignored = Fission_X86_64AsmEmitRex(buffer, 1, 0, -1, rmBits.Base)
        ignored = buffer.EmitByte(211)
        ignored = Fission_X86_64AsmEmitModRM(buffer, ext, right)
        RETURN
    END IF

    IF mnemonic == "jmp" ORELSE mnemonic == "call" THEN
        opcode = 233
        IF mnemonic == "call" THEN opcode = 232
        ignored = buffer.EmitByte(opcode)
        fieldOffset = buffer.Length()
        ignored = buffer.EmitU32(0)
        ignored = Array.Push(fixups, FissionX86_64Fixup(fieldOffset, operands[0].Name))
        RETURN
    END IF

    jccOpcodes = {"je": 132, "jz": 132, "jne": 133, "jnz": 133, "jl": 140, "jle": 142,
                  "jg": 143, "jge": 141, "js": 136, "jns": 137}
    IF Object.Has(jccOpcodes, mnemonic) THEN
        opcode = Object.Get(jccOpcodes, mnemonic, 132)
        ignored = buffer.EmitByte(15)
        ignored = buffer.EmitByte(opcode)
        fieldOffset = buffer.Length()
        ignored = buffer.EmitU32(0)
        ignored = Array.Push(fixups, FissionX86_64Fixup(fieldOffset, operands[0].Name))
        RETURN
    END IF

    IF mnemonic == "syscall" THEN
        ignored = buffer.EmitByte(15)
        ignored = buffer.EmitByte(5)
        RETURN
    END IF
    IF mnemonic == "ret" THEN
        ignored = buffer.EmitByte(195)
        RETURN
    END IF
    IF mnemonic == "leave" THEN
        ignored = buffer.EmitByte(201)
        RETURN
    END IF

    ignored = diagnostics.ReportError("FISSION_X86_64_ASM_UNSUPPORTED", "Unsupported instruction mnemonic for the self-contained assembler: " + mnemonic)
END FUNCTION

' Reverses Fission_X86_64EscapeAscii's own escaping (fission/amir/
' lower_x86_64.abas) -- a `.asciz`/`.ascii` directive's own quoted text
' still carries literal two-character `\"`/`\\`/`\n`/`\t`/`\r` escape
' sequences exactly the way a real GAS `.asciz` string would, since this
' backend's own codegen never changed how it renders that text, only how
' the RESULT is consumed. Returns a plain array of byte values (0-255).
FUNCTION Fission_X86_64AsmUnescapeBytes(text)
    chars = String.ToChars(text)
    bytes = []
    index = 0
    WHILE index < LEN(chars)
        ch = chars[index]
        IF ch == "\\" ANDALSO index + 1 < LEN(chars) THEN
            nextCh = chars[index + 1]
            IF nextCh == "\"" THEN
                ignored = Array.Push(bytes, 34)
            ELSE
                IF nextCh == "\\" THEN
                    ignored = Array.Push(bytes, 92)
                ELSE
                    IF nextCh == "n" THEN
                        ignored = Array.Push(bytes, 10)
                    ELSE
                        IF nextCh == "t" THEN
                            ignored = Array.Push(bytes, 9)
                        ELSE
                            IF nextCh == "r" THEN
                                ignored = Array.Push(bytes, 13)
                            ELSE
                                ignored = Array.Push(bytes, Fission_X86_64AsmCharCode(nextCh))
                            END IF
                        END IF
                    END IF
                END IF
            END IF
            index = index + 2
            CONTINUE WHILE
        END IF
        ignored = Array.Push(bytes, Fission_X86_64AsmCharCode(ch))
        index = index + 1
    WEND
    RETURN bytes
END FUNCTION

' A plain ASCII byte value for a single-character string -- every string
' constant this backend's own codegen ever renders is plain ASCII source
' text (confirmed by the same real-fixture inventory this whole file is
' scoped to), so a small fixed table covering the printable ASCII range
' plus the handful of control characters Fission_X86_64EscapeAscii itself
' ever needs to escape is enough; anything else falls back to 63 ('?')
' rather than silently emitting a wrong byte for a codepoint this backend
' was never asked to round-trip.
FUNCTION Fission_X86_64AsmCharCode(ch)
    table = String.ToChars(" !\"#$%&'()*+,-./0123456789:;<=>?@ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ[\\]^_`abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz{|}~")
    index = 0
    WHILE index < LEN(table)
        IF table[index] == ch THEN RETURN 32 + index
        index = index + 1
    WEND
    RETURN 63
END FUNCTION

FUNCTION Fission_X86_64AsmRoundUp(value, align)
    remainder = value BITAND (align - 1)
    IF remainder == 0 THEN RETURN value
    RETURN value + (align - remainder)
END FUNCTION

' Splits an already-trimmed instruction/directive line into its mnemonic
' and (still top-level-comma-joined) operand text, e.g.
' "mov %rdx, 8(%rax,%rcx,8)" -> {Mnemonic: "mov", OperandsText: "%rdx, 8(%rax,%rcx,8)"}.
FUNCTION Fission_X86_64AsmSplitMnemonic(trimmedLine)
    spaceIndex = String.IndexOf(trimmedLine, " ")
    IF spaceIndex < 0 THEN RETURN {Mnemonic: trimmedLine, OperandsText: ""}
    mnemonic = String.Slice(trimmedLine, 0, spaceIndex)
    rest = String.Trim(String.Slice(trimmedLine, spaceIndex + 1, String.Length(trimmedLine) - spaceIndex - 1))
    RETURN {Mnemonic: mnemonic, OperandsText: rest}
END FUNCTION

' The real encoder entry point: parses `assemblyText` (the exact text
' fission/amir/lower_x86_64.abas's own Fission_AmirToX86_64 already
' produces -- this backend's own self-defined dialect, not general GAS)
' into real machine code, packaged as a real, independent FRAGMENT (see
' fission/amir/x86_64_fragment.abas) -- text/rodata bytes, every label
' this text DEFINES as a real symbol, and every rel32/RIP-relative 4-byte
' field left as a zero placeholder recorded as a real relocation naming
' its own target label. This function does NOT resolve any label to a
' final address or write anything ELF-shaped at all -- that is
' fission/amir/fusion_linker.abas's own job (The Arcology Fusion Linker),
' entirely separate from instruction encoding. Returns
' {Ok, Fragment, Diagnostics}.
FUNCTION Fission_X86_64AssembleFragment(assemblyText)
    diagnostics = FissionDiagnosticBag()
    textBuffer = FissionX86_64Buffer()
    rodataBuffer = FissionX86_64Buffer()
    textFixups = []
    symbols = []
    bssOffset = 0
    currentSection = "text"

    lines = String.Split(assemblyText, "\n")
    FOR rawLine IN lines
        IF String.Trim(rawLine) == "" THEN CONTINUE FOR
        isLabel = (String.StartsWith(rawLine, "    ") == FALSE) ANDALSO String.EndsWith(String.Trim(rawLine), ":")
        IF isLabel THEN
            trimmed = String.Trim(rawLine)
            name = String.Slice(trimmed, 0, String.Length(trimmed) - 1)
            IF currentSection == "text" THEN ignored = Array.Push(symbols, {Name: name, Section: "text", Offset: textBuffer.Length()})
            IF currentSection == "rodata" THEN ignored = Array.Push(symbols, {Name: name, Section: "rodata", Offset: rodataBuffer.Length()})
            IF currentSection == "bss" THEN ignored = Array.Push(symbols, {Name: name, Section: "bss", Offset: bssOffset})
            CONTINUE FOR
        END IF

        split = Fission_X86_64AsmSplitMnemonic(String.Trim(rawLine))
        mnemonic = split.Mnemonic
        operandsText = split.OperandsText

        IF mnemonic == ".section" THEN
            currentSection = String.Slice(operandsText, 1, String.Length(operandsText) - 1)
            CONTINUE FOR
        END IF
        IF mnemonic == ".globl" THEN CONTINUE FOR

        IF mnemonic == ".asciz" ORELSE mnemonic == ".ascii" THEN
            quoted = String.Slice(operandsText, 1, String.Length(operandsText) - 2)
            bytes = Fission_X86_64AsmUnescapeBytes(quoted)
            FOR b IN bytes
                ignored = rodataBuffer.EmitByte(b)
            NEXT
            IF mnemonic == ".asciz" THEN ignored = rodataBuffer.EmitByte(0)
            CONTINUE FOR
        END IF
        IF mnemonic == ".byte" THEN
            ignored = rodataBuffer.EmitByte(NUMBER(operandsText))
            CONTINUE FOR
        END IF
        IF mnemonic == ".align" THEN
            IF currentSection == "bss" THEN bssOffset = Fission_X86_64AsmRoundUp(bssOffset, NUMBER(operandsText))
            CONTINUE FOR
        END IF
        IF mnemonic == ".skip" THEN
            IF currentSection == "bss" THEN bssOffset = bssOffset + NUMBER(operandsText)
            CONTINUE FOR
        END IF

        IF currentSection != "text" THEN
            ignored = diagnostics.ReportError("FISSION_X86_64_ASM_UNSUPPORTED", "Real instruction found outside .text: " + mnemonic)
            CONTINUE FOR
        END IF
        operandTokens = []
        IF operandsText != "" THEN operandTokens = Fission_X86_64AsmSplitTopLevel(operandsText, ",")
        index = 0
        WHILE index < LEN(operandTokens)
            operandTokens[index] = String.Trim(operandTokens[index])
            index = index + 1
        WEND
        ignored = Fission_X86_64AsmEncodeInstruction(textBuffer, textFixups, diagnostics, mnemonic, operandTokens)
    NEXT

    IF diagnostics.HasErrors() THEN RETURN {Ok: FALSE, Fragment: NULL, Diagnostics: diagnostics}

    ' Every fixup this pass recorded (Fission_X86_64AsmEncodeInstruction's
    ' own {FieldOffset, Target} shape, added the moment a jmp/call/lea
    ' needed a label it can't yet resolve) becomes a real relocation --
    ' always Section "text" here, since every rel32/RIP-relative field
    ' this backend's own codegen ever emits lives in .text (see
    ' fission/amir/x86_64_fragment.abas's own header comment on why that's
    ' sound, modeled generally rather than assumed forever). Every
    ' relocation this encoder itself ever produces is RIP-relative
    ' ("PC32", Addend -4 -- see fission/amir/fusion_linker.abas's own
    ' comment on why that specific formula/addend is real ELF's own
    ' R_X86_64_PC32/PLT32 convention, not a special case this backend
    ' invented) -- Type/Addend are explicit fields here (not left to
    ' Fusion's own default) so a genuine ELF object file's own relocations
    ' (fission/amir/elf_object.abas), which can carry a DIFFERENT type
    ' (R_X86_64_32, absolute) or addend, are handled by the exact same
    ' general patch logic with no special-casing for "which kind of
    ' fragment produced this."
    relocations = []
    FOR fixup IN textFixups
        ignored = Array.Push(relocations, {Section: "text", FieldOffset: fixup.FieldOffset, Target: fixup.Target, Type: "PC32", Addend: -4})
    NEXT

    fragment = FissionX86_64Fragment(textBuffer.Bytes, rodataBuffer.Bytes, bssOffset, symbols, relocations)
    RETURN {Ok: TRUE, Fragment: fragment, Diagnostics: diagnostics}
END FUNCTION
